## Entry and transaction contract

ReserveQueuedWithin(ctx context.Context, q transaction.Executor, a Attempt,
    intent JobIntent, workspaces []string, read QueueReader) (bool, error)
QueueReader func(context.Context, transaction.Executor) ([]QueueEntry, error)
ErrQueueTurnPending = SCHEDULING_QUEUE_TURN_PENDING

Borrow the selected owner's READ COMMITTED write executor. Queue admission
is the first scheduling write. Retain current actor/Workspace/node/selected-job
and physical fences. Supply the complete server-authorized domain and complete
bounded current eligible batch through that same executor. Persisted authority
resolves priority and positive sequence. Do not filter the returned batch by an
earlier domain. The callback takes no other jobs' row locks, changes no state,
opens no other transaction and calls no external service.

A current head reuses ReserveWithin and its borrowing/reclaim barriers. True is a
provisional logical hold. Commit dequeue, tasks, attempts, physical holds and audit
with it before success. False/nil is exact held replay, skips the dequeued owner
row read and must not create another task. Roll back on any error. Unknown commit
exposes no success; retry the exact identity.

## Fence protocol

Policy shared -> tenant -> selected workspace -> optional cohort.
Ordinary reserve/release/reclaim take tenant shared; queued admission takes
exclusive. Do not upgrade a prior shared scheduling fence in one transaction.
All Control writers must adopt before activation; mixed-version atomic queue
admission is not claimed. Other tenants remain independent; hash collisions
serialize. No private pool, new production DDL, route or dispatcher is installed.
ADR 0073 records the decision; main's ARC 0071/0072 remain intact.

